      "worked": "The domain excludes $x=-2$, so $(x+2)^2>0$.\nFor the left-hand inequality, multiply by $(x+2)^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}-(x+2)^2&<x(x+2)\\\\x(x+2)+(x+2)^2&>0\\\\2(x+2)(x+1)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThis gives $x<-2$ or $x>-1$.\nFor the right-hand inequality, multiply by $(x+2)^2$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x+2)&\\le3(x+2)^2\\\\3(x+2)^2-x(x+2)&\\ge0\\\\2(x+2)(x+3)&\\ge0\\end{align*}$$\nThis gives $x\\le-3$ or $x\\ge-2$; the domain removes $x=-2$.\nIntersecting both sets gives $x\\le-3$ or $x>-1$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
